[Music]  two of the men held responsible for one  of the deadliest nightclub fires in u.s  history are telling their side of the  story for the first time on tv club  owners jeff and michael derdarion faced  involuntary manslaughter charges after  100 people died and more than 200 people  were hurt in the 2003 fire it broke out  during a rock concert at the rhode  island nightclub the station for 48  hours jim axelrod spoke with some of the  survivors and learned some new  information that may help explain how  this tragedy happened  on february 20th 2003 at around 11 35 pm  jody king arrived at the station  nightclub in west warwick rhode island  his brother tracy worked there as a  bouncer  i see the horror and it was ugly the  roof was caving in walls were caving in  body after body in front of me  i don't even like to talk about  the fire started less than an hour  earlier when the band jack russell's  great white took the stage and their  tour manager set off four large  fireworks flames soon appeared on the  walls on either side and then it just  kept it kept growing jeff daddarian and  his brother michael owned the club it  was happening so fast fast fast fast  that's all i just can keep seeing in my  head  and the the the roof and just everything  just  passed too fast a hundred people  perished including jody's brother  over 200 people were injured we're sorry  for all of it and if we could change it  we would  nine months after the fire the dadarian  brothers along with daniel beakley great  white's tour manager were each charged  with 200 counts of involuntary  manslaughter they all eventually took  plea deals beakley and michael didarion  served time in prison we never knew the  whole story  because the trial never happened  so everything really never came out but  now 18 years later the brothers say they  want to set the record straight  why are you sitting here talking to me  we  wanted the full story to come out not  just some of it and that for people who  want to come to their own conclusion  on what happened that night  jim maxwell joins us right now jim why  did the nightclub burn down so quickly  right that's the key to the entire story  how quickly and how widely the flames  spread the brothers had received  complaints from their neighbors about  the sound coming out of the club so they  decided to install some foam on the  walls of the club to dampen the sound  problem is that foam was an accelerant  it spread it almost was described to me  as hanging solid gasoline on the walls  of the club but did they know that it  doesn't seem like that they would have  installed it if they knew that it could  be that dangerous crucial point this  will get into a lot tomorrow night on 48  hours but key point is the brother said  they ordered non-flammable sound foam  but got highly flammable packing foam  they produced the facts that showed  their order requested the sound foam and  this is a key critical part of the story  and part of this new information we'll  get into tomorrow night wow jim thank  you so much and speaking of tomorrow you  can watch jim's report the station  nightclub fire who's responsible  tomorrow night on 48 hours at 10 9  central right here on cbs

